Icons from the Breeze icon theme (KDE, breeze-icons 5.115), LGPL-3.0-or-later.
Source: https://invent.kde.org/frameworks/breeze-icons
Rendered from Breeze's SVGs with tools/breeze-icons.py. Coloured designs are favoured over Breeze's
monochrome glyphs: each icon is rendered from a coloured design if it has one at any size, else from
its monochrome ones; among those, the design made for its size, or else the next larger one. So the
small folder, computer, drive, document and dialog icons are Breeze's coloured ones scaled down.
The names are freedesktop.org's, as in the Oxygen set beside this one:
media-cdrom is Breeze's media-optical, system-installer its system-software-install,
battery-low its battery-020 (Breeze's own battery-low is the same as its battery-040), and the
battery-charging-* ones its battery-*-charging (battery-charging is battery-100-charging).
Breeze's emblem-favorite and clock are monochrome only, so emblem-favorite is its coloured
folder-favorites and clock its coloured preferences-system-time.
fluxos.png is the fluxOS logo (assets/fluxos-logo.svg, made by tools/mklogo.py), not part of
Breeze. wave.png is the Wave browser icon, rendered from assets/wave.svg (user-supplied artwork),
also not part of Breeze; both are the same files as in the Oxygen set.
